# changed texts (existing handles: text replaced, version +1)
@loca hc49689c0g291cg629bg2075g0bbfb07af743 Creatures you set on Fortune's wheel move one position at the start of your turn - <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="KINGMAKER_RISING">Rising</LSTag>, <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="KINGMAKER_REIGNING">Reigning</LSTag>, <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="KINGMAKER_FALLING">Falling</LSTag>, <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="KINGMAKER_FALLEN">Fallen</LSTag>, and round again. They stay on the Wheel until they die, combat ends or you cut their thread.<br><br>The ally that has Reigned the longest wears the crown as the <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="KINGMAKER_KING">King</LSTag>, and keeps it - even off the Wheel - until another ally has Reigned longer.
@loca he8aeaef6ge103gb1eeg33bfg1739036090df When an enemy on the Wheel becomes <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="KINGMAKER_FALLEN">Fallen</LSTag>, it takes [2] for each ally on the Wheel <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="KINGMAKER_REIGNING">Reigning</LSTag> within [1]. When an ally on the Wheel becomes Reigning, each Fallen enemy within [1] of it takes [2]. Each ally does this to an enemy only once per round.
@loca h98a1667ag257bg89c1g3a7bg812ce656a521 An enemy that begins <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="KINGMAKER_REIGNING">Reigning</LSTag> on the Wheel gains <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="KINGMAKER_HUBRIS">Hubris</LSTag>. The higher it climbs, the harder it falls - its next <LSTag Type="Passive" Tooltip="Arcana_Passive_TheCrossing">Crossing</LSTag> deals [1] instead.
@loca hbf648abdgae22gea64g24cegda87df7bc3d1 Climbed too high. The next Crossing it suffers deals [1] instead.
@loca h8056fb4fgea1fg274cg6ef6gd12ea0f42956 Lay Fallen while an ally reigned nearby, and took Force damage.
@loca h6151f413g0c66gb00bg764agd7b88239daf0 Your Crossings no longer need an ally nearby: every ally on the Wheel that is Reigning counts, wherever it stands.
@loca h3b48dcb1g0180geefbg8b4cgd0eb5735c31c Wears the crown of Fortune's wheel, on the Wheel or off it, until another ally has Reigned longer. The Kingmaker's Court serves the King.
@loca h3c47e40ag0ca9g7ee5g3da5g7fc7b9ec55ff Name your Court. Each ally you appoint holds an office until your next <LSTag Tooltip="LongRest">Long Rest</LSTag>. An office holder can never be the King or a Regent.
@loca hf5ce5edag27cdgeb7cg6ab0g0dd731cae197 Serves as the King's Hand and never wears the crown. While there is no King, or the King is not Reigning, lands a <LSTag Tooltip="CriticalHit">Critical Hit</LSTag> on a roll of 19 or 20.
@loca hae806e9bg81e9gff5dgdadfg62be7fc047d4 Appoint an ally as the King's Hand. It never wears the crown, but while there is no King, or the King is not Reigning, it lands a <LSTag Tooltip="CriticalHit">Critical Hit</LSTag> on a roll of 19 or 20.
@loca h8312755bg6e76g27d3g11f6gb268c41fc2c2 Carries the Crossing across the field: an enemy within [1] that becomes Fallen suffers one more Crossing, as if a Reigning ally stood beside it.
@loca h859f8ee7g4399gc9cbg6818gca91d9e2d9b5 Appoint an ally as Master of Ships. An enemy within [1] of it that becomes Fallen suffers one more Crossing, as if a Reigning ally stood beside it.
